.TH "CPS-FETCH" 1 "" "CPS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&cps\-fetch \- \&Fetch the verified payloads required by a saved plan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP 4
.B \&cps fetch [OPTIONS] <PLAN>
.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
.B \&<PLAN>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \&\-\-root <IMAGE>
\&Operate on this offline image instead of the running system
.TP
.B \&\-\-config <CONFIG>
\&Distribution configuration of the running system [default: /etc/cps/image.kdl]
.TP
.B \&\-\-archive\-cache <PUBLISHER=PATH>
\&Use a synced historical archive for pinned metadata and matching payloads
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B \&0
\&Success. A check found nothing to report.
.TP
.B \&1
\&An error.
.TP
.B \&2
\&Invalid usage, such as an unknown option or a missing argument.
.TP
.B \&3
\&A check found something: updates are available (upgrade \-\-check), verification found problems (verify, publisher audit\-builds), pins are stale (recipe repin \-\-check), configuration or images differ (config diff, image diff), manifest dependencies are missing (manifest dependencies), or nothing matched (search, owner).
.TP
.B \&4
\&A confirmation prompt was declined.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cps (1)
